                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Unwinding the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/whiskering"} whiskering
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              here, the claim follows, as indicated by the label of the upper 2-morphisms on the right.
            %p
              One observes now that these extra labels
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              are precisely the information that “trivializes” the conjugation action which in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomsBetweenBGs"}
              prevents the bare set of group homomorphism: a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi_1, h_1) \Rightarrow (\phi_2,h_2)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Grp
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp^{\ast/}
              is a natural isomorphism of groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi H
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi id
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\phi_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}H
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{id}}\downarrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\mathrlap{h}}&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{id}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    \&amp;\underset{\phi_2}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}H
                    }
            %p
              (encoding a conjugation relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Ad
                      %mi h
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_2 = Ad_{h} \circ \phi_1
              as above) such that we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
